1
00:00:01,876 --> 00:00:03,377
This is Lorelei Martins.

2
00:00:03,503 --> 00:00:06,255
She's a confederate
of the serial killer Red John.

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:10,301
Nineteen days ago she disappeared
from Sacramento County Jail.

4
00:00:10,593 --> 00:00:15,473
She was last seen in Wing B
Cell 826 at three-thirty PM.

5
00:00:16,724 --> 00:00:18,267
What does this have to do with me?

6
00:00:18,976 --> 00:00:20,645
Someone drove her out of the jail.

7
00:00:21,145 --> 00:00:24,106
The only vehicles that entered
the facility near that time

8
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:26,609
were prisoner transport vehicles.

9
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,778
You were driving one of them.

10
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:30,655
Was it you?

11
00:00:31,989 --> 00:00:33,032
No.

12
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:36,911
Hey.

13
00:00:37,245 --> 00:00:38,454
Was it you?

14
00:00:38,829 --> 00:00:40,623
No, all right?

15
00:00:45,878 --> 00:00:49,632
- What's wrong with you?
- You can go. Thank you.

16
00:01:17,076 --> 00:01:18,494
Morning, Lisbon.

17
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:20,580
Now?

18
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:23,791
Well, I... I have another driver coming in.

19
00:01:24,875 --> 00:01:26,460
Yeah. Okay.

20
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:28,421
Fine. I'll be right there.

21
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:52,445
Hey, Boss.

22
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:54,864
Victim's a community security guard.

23
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:56,032
Casey Borras.

24
00:01:56,157 --> 00:01:58,159
Shot twice, one in the arm
one in the chest.

25
00:01:58,284 --> 00:01:59,410
Happened about an hour ago.

26
00:01:59,535 --> 00:02:00,661
We've notified his family.

27
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:03,664
His weapon was out?
Was he responding to a call?

28
00:02:03,789 --> 00:02:05,833
No. Security company
says he was on patrol.

29
00:02:05,958 --> 00:02:07,877
Could've come across
a robbery or home invasion.

30
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:09,337
Sac PD's doing door-to-doors.

31
00:02:10,504 --> 00:02:11,881
Jane? Thoughts?

32
00:02:13,257 --> 00:02:16,135
Uh, no.

33
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:18,679
Gather the neighbors.

34
00:02:24,018 --> 00:02:27,396
I was in the den checking my Facebook
messages when I heard the shots.

35
00:02:27,521 --> 00:02:29,106
And, there were, like, two of them.

36
00:02:29,649 --> 00:02:30,816
Did you see anything?

37
00:02:30,941 --> 00:02:34,153
No. By the time I came outside
whoever did this was gone.

38
00:02:34,278 --> 00:02:38,699
- And what about you, sir?
- No, I just got home about ten minutes ago.

39
00:02:38,991 --> 00:02:42,078
Did anybody see any suspicious
people or vehicles?

40
00:02:42,203 --> 00:02:43,287
Anything at all?

41
00:02:46,874 --> 00:02:49,043
- What's going on with you?
- What?

42
00:02:49,251 --> 00:02:51,462
Everyone else here wants to help.
You just wanna get out of here.

43
00:02:51,587 --> 00:02:54,131
- No, I don't.
- Can't keep your eyes off your phone.

44
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:57,218
- What's your name?
- Isaac. Isaac Goodwin.

45
00:02:57,343 --> 00:03:00,221
- Which house is yours?
- I don't live in this neighborhood.

46
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:02,264
My brother and his wife do.
Right over there.

47
00:03:02,598 --> 00:03:03,683
Where are they?

48
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:06,394
Out of town.
I'm collecting their mail.

49
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:07,853
No, you're not.

50
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:09,438
Excuse me?

51
00:03:09,563 --> 00:03:13,567
You... You're in high finance. You're
a banker, a hedge fund manager, yes?

52
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:15,486
- Yes.
- You don't do favors for people

53
00:03:15,611 --> 00:03:17,321
unless there's something in it for you.

54
00:03:18,155 --> 00:03:20,449
- That's not true.
- Is the mailbox empty or full?

55
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:22,410
- I, uh...
- Say no more.

56
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:25,705
Go on.

57
00:03:33,045 --> 00:03:34,380
I don't know what you think
you're gonna find.

58
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:36,298
Well, how about evidence of a struggle?

59
00:03:37,466 --> 00:03:38,968
It must be the movers.

60
00:03:39,343 --> 00:03:41,053
Marcus and Pella
just got some new furniture.

61
00:03:41,178 --> 00:03:42,555
Remind me not to hire them.

62
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,306
Where are your brother and his wife now?

63
00:03:44,473 --> 00:03:46,684
I don't know.
Sometimes they just leave town.

64
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,728
They're spontaneous.
Where is he going?

65
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,483
I thought you stopped by to collect the mail.

66
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:56,152
I got hungry.

67
00:03:58,028 --> 00:04:00,781
Eh, hungry enough for two, it seems.

68
00:04:02,074 --> 00:04:04,410
- What's going on?
- Nothing.

69
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:07,163
We're not leaving until you tell us
what happened.

70
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:13,836
No. Don't answer that.

71
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:16,297
- Why not?
- Just don't. Give it to me.

72
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:17,798
- Well, tell me.
- I can't.

73
00:04:17,923 --> 00:04:19,300
- Well, if you don't, I'm gonna answer it.
- Don't!

74
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:21,761
- He told me not to involve the police.
- Who did?

75
00:04:22,678 --> 00:04:23,971
The kidnapper.

76
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:27,933
He took Marcus and Pella and he told me
he'd kill them if I involved the police.

77
00:04:28,058 --> 00:04:29,101
Better answer it, then.

78
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:32,730
- Hello?
- "You alone?"

79
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:37,026
- Yes.
- "Tell me, what are you wearing?"

80
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:43,199
Hi, how are you doing? It's me.
Yeah.

81
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:47,995
Okay.
We can just talk now... kidnappers.

82
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:03,509
The River Park neighborhood
of Sacramento

83
00:05:03,634 --> 00:05:04,718
where local security guard...

84
00:05:04,843 --> 00:05:06,970
All right, we're dealing
with a kidnapping.

85
00:05:07,554 --> 00:05:09,640
The victims are Pella
and Marcus Goodwin.

86
00:05:09,765 --> 00:05:11,558
They were taken about 90 minutes ago.

87
00:05:11,683 --> 00:05:14,019
{\an8}It looks like a security guard
came across the scene

88
00:05:14,144 --> 00:05:16,021
{\an8}tried to intervene, and was shot.

89
00:05:16,146 --> 00:05:18,315
{\an8}So we find the kidnapper
we've got the killer.

90
00:05:18,524 --> 00:05:21,235
{\an8}But right now our priority is
getting the Goodwins back safely.

91
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,486
{\an8}Has the kidnapper made contact?

92
00:05:22,694 --> 00:05:24,988
{\an8}He emailed the brother around
the time of abduction.

93
00:05:25,113 --> 00:05:27,449
Isaac Goodwin came to the house
to verify it was true.

94
00:05:27,616 --> 00:05:29,952
- What about a ransom demand?
- Five million dollars.

95
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,203
They got that kind of money?

96
00:05:31,328 --> 00:05:34,873
{\an8}Isaac says Marcus is the chief designer
at a communication software firm.

97
00:05:34,998 --> 00:05:37,334
{\an8}He's got big government contracts
and holds major patents.

98
00:05:37,459 --> 00:05:38,794
{\an8}So, yes, he's got the money.

99
00:05:39,461 --> 00:05:41,171
{\an8}The kidnapper's supposed
to be in touch within the hour.

100
00:05:41,296 --> 00:05:42,631
Van Pelt's in the kitchen setting up.

101
00:05:42,798 --> 00:05:43,841
I'll put out a BOLO.

102
00:05:43,966 --> 00:05:46,635
Rigsby, I need you to check all
the security camera footage in the area.

103
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:50,097
{\an8}Traffic lights, residential, anything that
can put an ID on our suspect.

104
00:05:50,264 --> 00:05:51,682
{\an8}The clock's ticking, let's move.

105
00:05:51,807 --> 00:05:52,933
{\an8}- Yes, boss.
- Yes, boss.

106
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,103
{\an8}What now?

107
00:06:14,454 --> 00:06:15,831
Great system, huh?

108
00:06:18,292 --> 00:06:19,543
Could you turn that off?

109
00:06:19,668 --> 00:06:22,421
{\an8}Sure, sure, hang on a second.
Uh...

110
00:06:26,925 --> 00:06:28,594
{\an8}It's a little harder than it looks.

111
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:31,513
{\an8}We're gonna need to put
together the ransom.

112
00:06:31,638 --> 00:06:32,681
{\an8}Can you help with that?

113
00:06:34,391 --> 00:06:37,185
{\an8}Yes. I'm Marcus' business manager.

114
00:06:37,519 --> 00:06:38,729
{\an8}Why the hesitation?

115
00:06:39,313 --> 00:06:41,481
{\an8}Well, it's five million dollars.

116
00:06:41,607 --> 00:06:44,026
{\an8}I'm not just gonna go to the bank
and then hand it over to them.

117
00:06:44,151 --> 00:06:46,028
{\an8}I mean, there has to be
a negotiation first.

118
00:06:46,153 --> 00:06:47,487
{\an8}Which we will run.

119
00:06:47,613 --> 00:06:48,739
{\an8}And we're gonna need your phone.

120
00:06:48,906 --> 00:06:51,366
{\an8}The kidnapper contacted you.
He'll probably do so again.

121
00:06:51,491 --> 00:06:52,784
{\an8}Okay, maybe I wasn't clear before.

122
00:06:52,951 --> 00:06:56,914
{\an8}If he knows that you guys are involved
then Marcus and Pella are dead.

123
00:06:57,039 --> 00:06:59,166
{\an8}I have to protect my family.
They're all I have.

124
00:06:59,791 --> 00:07:03,420
{\an8}I understand your concern
but this is a police matter now.

125
00:07:03,545 --> 00:07:05,505
{\an8}We're gonna deal
with the kidnapper from here on out.

126
00:07:06,924 --> 00:07:10,719
No. No, I'm not gonna have their
blood on my hands, okay?

127
00:07:11,053 --> 00:07:12,471
{\an8}Hard to argue with that.

128
00:07:12,596 --> 00:07:15,182
{\an8}You are not leaving this house
with that phone.

129
00:07:15,807 --> 00:07:17,351
{\an8}Fine. I'll stay.

130
00:07:17,684 --> 00:07:19,102
{\an8}But nobody's touching my phone.

131
00:07:22,481 --> 00:07:24,524
{\an8}Mm. Good luck with that.

132
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:29,696
{\an8}Mr. Goodwin.

133
00:07:33,992 --> 00:07:35,535
{\an8}Mr. Goodwin, open up.

134
00:07:37,204 --> 00:07:38,455
Open the door.

135
00:07:38,789 --> 00:07:41,625
"I'm c... I'm calling my lawyer.
I'm not talking until he gets here."

136
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:46,713
{\an8}Okay, we will break down this door
if we are forced to.

137
00:07:47,130 --> 00:07:49,758
{\an8}- I said, open up!
- Lisbon?

138
00:07:50,592 --> 00:07:51,718
Brenda.

139
00:07:52,219 --> 00:07:54,680
What are you doing here?
Is there a PR issue?

140
00:07:54,805 --> 00:07:55,847
Can I speak with you?

141
00:08:01,937 --> 00:08:03,647
Teresa, you can't break down that door.

142
00:08:03,897 --> 00:08:06,525
I need to access his email
and his phone.

143
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:08,527
Breaking down the door
is not my first option

144
00:08:08,652 --> 00:08:10,112
but I don't have time to pull a warrant.

145
00:08:10,237 --> 00:08:11,279
That may be the case

146
00:08:11,405 --> 00:08:14,408
but Director Bertram is very concerned
about the way we handle this one.

147
00:08:14,992 --> 00:08:17,619
We need to be very gentle
with the Goodwin family.

148
00:08:17,744 --> 00:08:19,705
- We'll discuss this later.
- No, we can't.

149
00:08:19,830 --> 00:08:21,498
Do you see those press vans pulling up?

150
00:08:21,665 --> 00:08:24,126
Marcus Goodwin is an important
advisor for the Pentagon.

151
00:08:24,292 --> 00:08:26,169
His disappearance is
a national security issue.

152
00:08:26,336 --> 00:08:28,088
If we don't get him and his wife back
do you know what happens?

153
00:08:28,213 --> 00:08:30,382
- We're gonna get him back.
- Yes, I'm sure that we will.

154
00:08:30,507 --> 00:08:33,093
But if we don't, and we treat Isaac badly
he's gonna kill us in the media.

155
00:08:33,385 --> 00:08:34,428
Kill us.

156
00:08:34,553 --> 00:08:35,971
You've got your problems, I've got mine.

157
00:08:36,805 --> 00:08:38,890
Well, then I'm sorry to do this
to you, Teresa.

158
00:08:39,016 --> 00:08:40,058
What are you doing?

159
00:08:40,183 --> 00:08:41,351
Calling Director Bertram.

160
00:08:44,396 --> 00:08:46,773
Fine. Uh, you win.

161
00:08:49,317 --> 00:08:50,360
Sorry.

162
00:08:58,201 --> 00:08:59,870
I'll tell if you steal one.

163
00:09:06,793 --> 00:09:08,086
Uh, may I see that?

164
00:09:12,132 --> 00:09:14,134
Whoa. That's odd.

165
00:09:14,885 --> 00:09:15,927
What?

166
00:09:16,053 --> 00:09:19,765
They drank a 1964
Lafite Rothschild with a pizza.

167
00:09:20,974 --> 00:09:22,017
So?

168
00:09:22,142 --> 00:09:23,351
Well, these people are wine snobs.

169
00:09:23,518 --> 00:09:26,897
They have varietal specific stemware.
They should know better.

170
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:36,490
Did you happen to see a dog anywhere?

171
00:09:37,657 --> 00:09:38,700
No.

172
00:09:39,951 --> 00:09:40,994
Howard?

173
00:09:41,953 --> 00:09:43,413
Where are you, boy?

174
00:09:52,547 --> 00:09:54,216
Isaac?

175
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:58,762
I talked it over with my boss
and you're right.

176
00:09:59,513 --> 00:10:02,349
You should be the one
to deal with the kidnapper.

177
00:10:03,266 --> 00:10:05,685
Nobody's gonna take your phone.

178
00:10:07,437 --> 00:10:10,190
I feel bad that you're you in there.

179
00:10:13,151 --> 00:10:15,153
- Isaac?
- "Lawyer."

180
00:10:28,291 --> 00:10:30,544
Hey, Howard. Come on.

181
00:10:33,130 --> 00:10:36,091
Oh, hey. Howard.
How you doing?

182
00:10:36,299 --> 00:10:40,762
Found old Howard lounging by my pool.
He's a sneaky one.

183
00:10:42,556 --> 00:10:45,851
- Does he get out a lot?
- No, but he tries.

184
00:10:46,017 --> 00:10:48,937
Marcus and Pella do a pretty good job
of keeping him on the property.

185
00:10:50,605 --> 00:10:53,108
- I bet it was that gate, wasn't it?
- Oh, why do you say that?

186
00:10:53,275 --> 00:10:54,860
Well, it's got a funny latch on it.

187
00:10:55,026 --> 00:10:56,736
And it's hard to close
if you're not used to it.

188
00:10:56,862 --> 00:10:57,904
Hm.

189
00:10:58,071 --> 00:10:59,531
Something about the Goodwins, huh?

190
00:11:00,407 --> 00:11:03,201
Yeah. Uh, do you think you
could watch Howard for me?

191
00:11:03,577 --> 00:11:05,954
- Oh, not at all.
- I really appreciate it. Thank you.

192
00:11:06,663 --> 00:11:07,706
See you, Howard.

193
00:11:20,802 --> 00:11:21,845
Jane!

194
00:11:23,722 --> 00:11:24,764
Just a minute!

195
00:11:51,124 --> 00:11:52,250
What are you doing?

196
00:11:57,797 --> 00:11:59,341
Lisbon. I got something.

197
00:11:59,633 --> 00:12:01,384
I need to get in touch with Isaac's lawyer.

198
00:12:01,509 --> 00:12:02,928
What, you still can't get him out of there?

199
00:12:03,053 --> 00:12:04,095
You can? Good luck.

200
00:12:04,554 --> 00:12:07,557
Yo, Isaac.
I got something to tell you.

201
00:12:07,682 --> 00:12:10,769
Marcus and Pella weren't kidnapped.
Somebody else was.

202
00:12:10,894 --> 00:12:13,146
- What? Who?
- Well, I don't know, but...

203
00:12:16,024 --> 00:12:20,612
Unlike Marcus and Pella, they don't know
their Bordeaux from cheap table plonk.

204
00:12:20,737 --> 00:12:24,574
And they listen to Country, not Opera.
And unfortunately, they let Howard out.

205
00:12:25,617 --> 00:12:26,660
What did you say?

206
00:12:26,785 --> 00:12:28,245
- Who the hell is Howard?
- Dog.

207
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:32,749
- Isaac? What's going on here?
- Marcus.

208
00:12:32,916 --> 00:12:34,834
Well... We thought you were kidnapped.

209
00:12:35,669 --> 00:12:36,962
Well, not all of us.

210
00:12:43,665 --> 00:12:46,793
Uh, we've been hiking all weekend.
It was a last-minute trip.

211
00:12:46,918 --> 00:12:48,253
We were at our place in the mountains.

212
00:12:48,420 --> 00:12:51,840
There's no phone. No cell reception.
We had no idea.

213
00:12:51,965 --> 00:12:54,092
- Who was staying at the house?
- Gary and Sloan Dietz.

214
00:12:54,217 --> 00:12:55,510
We've been best friends
with them for years.

215
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:58,054
Marcus and Gary were
roommates at Cal-Tech.

216
00:12:58,180 --> 00:12:59,598
This is insane.

217
00:13:00,515 --> 00:13:03,643
- Do you have a photo of the couple?
- Um, yeah.

218
00:13:04,102 --> 00:13:07,522
They were, uh, house sitting.
We have a dog.

219
00:13:08,106 --> 00:13:10,650
Oh, great dog, by the way.
He's, uh, with the neighbor.

220
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:14,070
So the kidnapper has Gary and Sloan

221
00:13:14,237 --> 00:13:16,490
but he sent Isaac an email
saying that he has us?

222
00:13:16,781 --> 00:13:19,159
We think that maybe they took
the wrong couple by mistake.

223
00:13:19,326 --> 00:13:20,494
Well, obviously.

224
00:13:20,619 --> 00:13:24,247
But by now the kidnappers must've figured
out that they took the wrong people, so...

225
00:13:24,581 --> 00:13:27,292
I mean, what happens to Gary and Sloan?
Are they gonna get killed?

226
00:13:27,417 --> 00:13:28,960
Don't even say that.

227
00:13:29,127 --> 00:13:31,379
- I'm just being realistic.
- Isaac, shut up.

228
00:13:31,505 --> 00:13:34,049
Isaac's always been
the family scourge, hasn't he?

229
00:13:34,424 --> 00:13:39,054
- Stubborn, arrogant, insensitive.
- Hey, enough.

230
00:13:45,018 --> 00:13:47,562
Someone's trying to video conference.
It could be the kidnapper.

231
00:13:47,687 --> 00:13:49,606
I'm sending the feed to the laptop.

232
00:13:51,691 --> 00:13:55,403
- Oh, my God.
- "Who are you? Where's Isaac?"

233
00:13:55,529 --> 00:13:57,280
I'm with the police.
You're dealing with us now.

234
00:13:57,447 --> 00:13:58,823
"I said no police."

235
00:13:59,741 --> 00:14:00,784
Things have changed.

236
00:14:00,909 --> 00:14:03,203
"So you've figured out
I took the wrong people."

237
00:14:03,495 --> 00:14:05,497
"I'm guessing Marcus and Pella are there?"

238
00:14:05,622 --> 00:14:06,790
They're right here.

239
00:14:07,582 --> 00:14:10,126
"Good.
Because I have a question for them."

240
00:14:11,419 --> 00:14:13,588
"Do you wanna see your
friends alive again?"

241
00:14:13,713 --> 00:14:15,590
Yes. Yes, we'll do anything.

242
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:18,677
"Five million dollars
in non-sequential bills."

243
00:14:18,843 --> 00:14:22,889
"You have 24 hours to get it.
If you don't, your friends die."

244
00:14:23,473 --> 00:14:26,142
"I'll contact you in the morning
with instructions for delivery."

245
00:14:27,310 --> 00:14:29,187
Uh, quick question before you go.

246
00:14:29,312 --> 00:14:32,649
Uh, kidnapping Gary and Sloan wasn't
a mistake, was it?

247
00:14:32,774 --> 00:14:34,192
"What are you talking about?"

248
00:14:34,317 --> 00:14:37,779
Kidnapping Gary and Sloan was
always the plan, wasn't it?

249
00:14:37,904 --> 00:14:38,947
"No."

250
00:14:39,072 --> 00:14:41,116
You see, I think you did your homework.

251
00:14:41,241 --> 00:14:43,577
You wanted Marcus' money
but if you kidnapped him

252
00:14:43,702 --> 00:14:45,370
then you would have had
to deal with Isaac.

253
00:14:45,870 --> 00:14:48,415
Bullheaded guy like that, you'd be
lucky to get twenty bucks out of him.

254
00:14:48,999 --> 00:14:50,292
"Who is this?"

255
00:14:51,042 --> 00:14:53,795
Huh? But you did take Gary and Sloan

256
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:56,923
but you sent an email saying
you had Marcus and Pella.

257
00:14:57,132 --> 00:14:59,968
That way Marcus thinks
he's supposed to be taken.

258
00:15:00,135 --> 00:15:02,137
He feels wracked with guilt.

259
00:15:02,470 --> 00:15:05,974
And the nice guy that he is, he doesn't
think twice about dropping a few mil.

260
00:15:06,099 --> 00:15:07,183
You know him very well.

261
00:15:07,309 --> 00:15:08,518
"Shut up."

262
00:15:08,727 --> 00:15:11,771
"I want the five million or they die."

263
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:14,357
Oh, you're clever enough to know
that that's not gonna happen.

264
00:15:14,482 --> 00:15:16,443
You're selling beer now, not champagne.

265
00:15:16,818 --> 00:15:19,863
No one's gonna pay five million dollars.
Three, maybe.

266
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:22,073
- "It's five."
- Three's a better number.

267
00:15:22,198 --> 00:15:23,450
"Then people start dying."

268
00:15:24,951 --> 00:15:25,994
What did you do?

269
00:15:26,369 --> 00:15:27,704
He'll call back.

270
00:15:43,303 --> 00:15:44,346
Jane?

271
00:15:45,013 --> 00:15:46,056
Jane.

272
00:15:46,222 --> 00:15:49,184
- Don't worry. He'll call back.
- Then why do you look worried?

273
00:15:49,684 --> 00:15:50,810
I'm not.

274
00:15:51,895 --> 00:15:54,564
No luck tracing the email to Isaac
or the video conference.

275
00:15:54,689 --> 00:15:55,815
Have you heard from Cho and Rigsby?

276
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:58,276
They're still going through
the security camera footage.

277
00:15:59,861 --> 00:16:00,904
Told you.

278
00:16:05,408 --> 00:16:09,412
- "Four million. Final offer."
- Yeah, that's fine.

279
00:16:10,038 --> 00:16:12,957
- All right. Four million.
- "I'll contact you in the morning."

280
00:16:13,083 --> 00:16:15,335
Okay.
Isaac, let's get the money together.

281
00:16:16,336 --> 00:16:17,420
Are you kidding?

282
00:16:18,088 --> 00:16:19,673
Look, just because you guys
feel guilty

283
00:16:19,798 --> 00:16:21,883
doesn't mean you should give away
millions of dollars here.

284
00:16:22,008 --> 00:16:23,802
Gary's a high school physics teacher.
Sloan's a paralegal.

285
00:16:23,927 --> 00:16:25,053
They don't have this kind of cash.

286
00:16:25,178 --> 00:16:27,180
It's not your fault that Gary
isn't successful.

287
00:16:27,305 --> 00:16:28,932
- This is not your problem.
- Yeah, it is. Okay?

288
00:16:29,057 --> 00:16:30,892
Gary's family.
Now get the money.

289
00:16:31,226 --> 00:16:34,354
Oh. You don't have it, do you?

290
00:16:36,022 --> 00:16:37,816
What?
Of course he's got it.

291
00:16:41,611 --> 00:16:42,904
It's complicated.

292
00:16:43,488 --> 00:16:48,076
Look, the market has been unpredictable.

293
00:16:48,326 --> 00:16:51,079
And I have done the best
that I can possibly do

294
00:16:51,204 --> 00:16:55,208
but there have been
significant reversals.

295
00:16:56,209 --> 00:17:01,172
I've done my best, but most of it
is tied up in illiquid securities.

296
00:17:01,297 --> 00:17:02,757
But the books don't say that.

297
00:17:04,259 --> 00:17:06,261
Look, if you wanna get
the four million dollars

298
00:17:06,386 --> 00:17:08,096
then you're gonna have to start
selling off assets.

299
00:17:08,221 --> 00:17:10,014
And who knows how long
that's gonna take.

300
00:17:12,559 --> 00:17:15,270
I'm sorry, Marcus. I really am.

301
00:17:16,730 --> 00:17:18,106
You son of a bitch.

302
00:17:18,231 --> 00:17:21,109
I think you guys should just talk
amongst yourselves for a while.

303
00:17:21,234 --> 00:17:22,277
I'm out of here.

304
00:17:22,944 --> 00:17:25,196
- You're leaving?
- Yes. I have a driver coming in.

305
00:17:25,613 --> 00:17:26,990
Let me know how it goes.

306
00:17:37,709 --> 00:17:39,961
Will you please eat that like a human
being and not a sea lion?

307
00:17:44,007 --> 00:17:45,049
Hold on.

308
00:17:45,467 --> 00:17:46,551
I think I got something.

309
00:17:53,516 --> 00:17:55,310
Going pretty fast.
Where was that taken?

310
00:17:55,435 --> 00:17:57,729
A security camera three blocks
away from the Goodwin house.

311
00:17:57,854 --> 00:17:58,980
Could be our guy in the van.

312
00:18:03,067 --> 00:18:04,277
There's no license plate.

313
00:18:08,031 --> 00:18:11,284
And only 98000 white vans
registered in Northern California.

314
00:18:11,993 --> 00:18:14,329
Check for abandoned white vans.
Looks like a Dodge.

315
00:18:14,454 --> 00:18:15,497
See if that narrows it.

316
00:18:18,917 --> 00:18:20,126
Fifty-six.

317
00:18:22,212 --> 00:18:24,964
But one of them was found six miles from
the Goodwin house just a few hours ago.

318
00:18:25,089 --> 00:18:26,216
Reported stolen last week.

319
00:18:26,925 --> 00:18:28,760
Maybe the owner saw something.
Let's check it out.

320
00:18:28,968 --> 00:18:30,011
Okay.

321
00:18:32,096 --> 00:18:33,264
This is Lorelei Martins.

322
00:18:33,389 --> 00:18:36,142
She's a confederate
of the serial killer, Red John.

323
00:18:36,392 --> 00:18:40,104
Nineteen days ago, she disappeared
from Sacramento County Jail.

324
00:18:42,065 --> 00:18:43,441
Someone drove her out.

325
00:18:43,942 --> 00:18:44,984
Was it you?

326
00:18:46,236 --> 00:18:48,863
- You oughta check the log.
- I have.

327
00:18:49,197 --> 00:18:53,451
You realize I transport dozens
of prisoners every day.

328
00:18:54,619 --> 00:18:55,662
Sure.

329
00:19:10,927 --> 00:19:12,595
Never seen her in my life.

330
00:19:14,347 --> 00:19:16,015
- You're lying.
- Excuse me?

331
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:18,351
- You're lying.
- I don't have to listen to this.

332
00:19:19,060 --> 00:19:21,354
Sit, no... Sit... Please, sit down.

333
00:19:22,605 --> 00:19:24,023
You gonna make me?

334
00:19:25,275 --> 00:19:27,902
Wrong move, Walter. Just stay.

335
00:19:36,494 --> 00:19:38,746
I know, right?
It's like, "Hello?"

336
00:19:38,872 --> 00:19:40,707
"It's your birthday, ho. Cheer up."

337
00:19:44,085 --> 00:19:45,420
I gotta call you back, girl.

338
00:19:45,545 --> 00:19:48,756
I've got some Jehovah Witnesses
or something at the door.

339
00:19:50,592 --> 00:19:51,634
All right.

340
00:19:52,969 --> 00:19:54,012
CBI, ma'am.

341
00:19:54,178 --> 00:19:57,432
Your 2002 white Dodge van was
reported stolen last Wednesday.

342
00:19:57,557 --> 00:19:58,600
Mm-hm.

343
00:19:58,725 --> 00:20:01,853
- Any idea who might've taken it?
- Uh, no?

344
00:20:01,978 --> 00:20:04,522
If I did, dude would be rotting
in a cell about now.

345
00:20:06,566 --> 00:20:09,027
Is that 70 inches? Expensive.

346
00:20:12,405 --> 00:20:14,073
Mom's got glaucoma.

347
00:20:14,282 --> 00:20:16,326
Your van, it was ten years old
and in bad condition.

348
00:20:16,451 --> 00:20:17,827
It's an odd vehicle to steal, isn't it?

349
00:20:17,994 --> 00:20:19,829
And suddenly you have
the cash to buy a new TV.

350
00:20:19,996 --> 00:20:22,248
Listen, the longer you lie to us
the worse it's gonna be.

351
00:20:29,422 --> 00:20:31,049
All right, fine.

352
00:20:32,383 --> 00:20:35,637
It wasn't stolen. I sold it.

353
00:20:36,095 --> 00:20:37,138
To who?

354
00:20:37,722 --> 00:20:38,806
Don't know.

355
00:20:38,932 --> 00:20:40,183
Dude ain't give me his name.

356
00:20:40,308 --> 00:20:41,976
Didn't want me to sign
over the title either.

357
00:20:42,101 --> 00:20:48,858
But he gave me a couple thousand
extra, so I was like... All right.

358
00:20:49,609 --> 00:20:51,361
So why'd you report it stolen?

359
00:20:51,527 --> 00:20:55,198
I didn't know what he was gonna do
with that van, and it was still in my name.

360
00:20:55,740 --> 00:20:56,824
Mm-hm.

361
00:20:57,492 --> 00:20:58,910
Didn't want it coming back on me.

362
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:00,745
You need to come work
with our sketch artist.

363
00:21:00,870 --> 00:21:02,080
See if we can get a likeness of this man.

364
00:21:03,414 --> 00:21:08,044
If I help, can I keep the TV?

365
00:21:11,047 --> 00:21:12,090
Let's go.

366
00:21:12,757 --> 00:21:15,468
I was just asking. Ugh.

367
00:21:22,934 --> 00:21:24,185
Ma, I'm going.

368
00:21:29,190 --> 00:21:33,236
We've scraped together everything that
we can, and we're still a million short.

369
00:21:33,653 --> 00:21:35,446
Isaac's trying to sell some of our assets

370
00:21:35,571 --> 00:21:38,449
but even if he does, the money's
not gonna get here in time.

371
00:21:38,825 --> 00:21:41,452
We're just... We're at a loss.

372
00:21:41,619 --> 00:21:43,371
Even if by some miracle
we do get this money today

373
00:21:43,538 --> 00:21:45,957
how do we know that he's not still
gonna kill Gary and Sloan?

374
00:21:46,249 --> 00:21:47,583
Honestly, you never do.

375
00:21:47,709 --> 00:21:49,544
That has to be a risk
you're willing to take.

376
00:21:49,669 --> 00:21:51,713
No, we're willing.
Of course we're willing.

377
00:21:55,383 --> 00:21:56,426
This is it.

378
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:02,807
"Gary and Sloan are still alive.
How long, is up to you."

379
00:22:03,016 --> 00:22:06,060
- "Is the money ready?"
- Pella and Marcus need more time.

380
00:22:06,185 --> 00:22:07,228
"You're lying."

381
00:22:07,353 --> 00:22:09,856
They have every intention
of paying the money.

382
00:22:09,981 --> 00:22:12,984
"Stop lying to me, bitch.
I know they have it."

383
00:22:13,109 --> 00:22:16,529
Hey, just for that, you're not gonna
see a dime. Not until you do as I say.

384
00:22:16,779 --> 00:22:18,906
- "What?"
- Shut your mouth and you listen to me.

385
00:22:19,032 --> 00:22:21,075
I need to know you're not gonna kill
them after you get the cash.

386
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:22,243
So this is what you're gonna do.

387
00:22:22,368 --> 00:22:25,163
You're gonna release one hostage
in exactly one hour.

388
00:22:25,371 --> 00:22:27,707
- Consider it a show of good faith.
- "Wait, I..."

389
00:22:27,874 --> 00:22:30,418
You heard me! One hostage in one hour.

390
00:22:30,668 --> 00:22:32,545
And if you don't, don't bother calling back.

391
00:22:33,129 --> 00:22:34,172
What?

392
00:22:34,756 --> 00:22:39,093
- Boy, I think that was pretty convincing.
- You might've just gotten them killed.

393
00:22:49,333 --> 00:22:50,918
No video conference. Just a call.

394
00:22:55,439 --> 00:22:56,607
Hello?

395
00:22:59,902 --> 00:23:03,030
This is Sloan Dietz.
I was told to call this number.

396
00:23:04,699 --> 00:23:07,743
- Yeah?
- Please, help me.

397
00:23:09,662 --> 00:23:12,164
I'm sorry. I don't know anything.

398
00:23:12,373 --> 00:23:15,376
I'm not sure where he brought us.
We... we were blindfolded.

399
00:23:16,460 --> 00:23:19,046
Did you hear any distinctive
noises on the trip?

400
00:23:19,171 --> 00:23:20,631
Airplanes? Trains?

401
00:23:22,883 --> 00:23:26,262
I don't know. I don't... I don't remember.

402
00:23:26,637 --> 00:23:29,140
Everything happened so fast. I'm sorry.

403
00:23:29,599 --> 00:23:30,725
It's fine.

404
00:23:30,850 --> 00:23:31,934
Take a look at this.

405
00:23:32,602 --> 00:23:34,770
It's from a description of the kidnapper.

406
00:23:34,895 --> 00:23:35,938
Do you recognize him?

407
00:23:36,897 --> 00:23:39,317
No, uh... He never let us see his face.

408
00:23:45,406 --> 00:23:50,703
I'm not being very helpful at all.
I'm so sorry.

409
00:23:52,747 --> 00:23:54,206
Why don't we take a break?

410
00:23:59,211 --> 00:24:01,255
We need to find the money
to get Gary back.

411
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:02,757
That's what this comes down to.

412
00:24:03,716 --> 00:24:05,926
Well, what do you think, Isaac?

413
00:24:06,844 --> 00:24:09,972
It's not gonna happen this fast.
I'm doing everything that I can, but...

414
00:24:10,556 --> 00:24:13,309
Not everything. You could chip in.

415
00:24:13,893 --> 00:24:19,106
I want to. But a million dollars? That's...
That's almost everything that I have.

416
00:24:19,482 --> 00:24:20,816
Please, Isaac.

417
00:24:21,275 --> 00:24:25,071
Sloan, don't think that
I don't feel for you. I do.

418
00:24:25,363 --> 00:24:26,822
I will pay you back.

419
00:24:27,073 --> 00:24:30,493
Look, I know
how ridiculous that sounds

420
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:35,790
but I swear, trust me, I will work every
day for the rest of my life.

421
00:24:36,707 --> 00:24:38,250
I swear it.

422
00:24:39,585 --> 00:24:40,961
It's okay, Sloan.

423
00:24:41,504 --> 00:24:44,799
I'll pay you back, Isaac.
You know I'm good for it.

424
00:24:46,092 --> 00:24:47,385
Please.

425
00:24:49,428 --> 00:24:51,097
Don't let him die.

426
00:24:59,897 --> 00:25:01,232
We have the money.

427
00:25:01,649 --> 00:25:02,775
"Good."

428
00:25:03,025 --> 00:25:04,110
"Now listen carefully."

429
00:25:04,235 --> 00:25:07,655
"I want it tomorrow, ten a.m.
at the Village Plaza."

430
00:25:08,114 --> 00:25:11,867
"There's a table by the pretzel cart.
The wife will bring it there."

431
00:25:11,992 --> 00:25:14,203
Sloan?
That's not gonna happen.

432
00:25:14,370 --> 00:25:16,831
"I won't let you have some undercover
cop bring the money."

433
00:25:16,956 --> 00:25:18,541
"This is non-negotiable."

434
00:25:19,125 --> 00:25:20,501
"Don't push me."

435
00:25:20,626 --> 00:25:22,128
When can we get proof of life?

436
00:25:22,253 --> 00:25:23,546
"Nine AM."

437
00:25:24,004 --> 00:25:28,926
"If you disrupt the exchange, or if
I see a cop anywhere near that mall..."

438
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:32,138
I promise Gary is a dead man.

439
00:25:33,764 --> 00:25:35,099
Who's gonna tell Sloan?

440
00:25:35,474 --> 00:25:37,435
Well, I think you guys
can handle it from here.

441
00:25:42,606 --> 00:25:45,943
Hey. You never told me
what happened with the driver.

442
00:25:48,070 --> 00:25:50,656
Yeah, it's must've, uh...
slipped my mind.

443
00:25:50,781 --> 00:25:51,824
Excuse me.

444
00:25:52,992 --> 00:25:54,577
He knows something, doesn't he?

445
00:25:57,371 --> 00:25:58,873
Jane, let me help you.

446
00:26:01,584 --> 00:26:02,626
Thank you.

447
00:26:31,989 --> 00:26:34,450
"Harder. Harder."

448
00:27:12,321 --> 00:27:13,781
I don't know if I can
go through with this.

449
00:27:13,948 --> 00:27:15,366
We have the money ready for you.

450
00:27:16,909 --> 00:27:20,287
All you have to do is hand it over.
Piece of cake.

451
00:27:21,121 --> 00:27:22,414
I'll be outside if you need me, okay?

452
00:27:50,234 --> 00:27:52,570
- Hey, baby.
- "Hey."

453
00:27:54,864 --> 00:27:56,282
So? How'd it go?

454
00:27:56,949 --> 00:27:58,492
They don't have a clue.

455
00:27:59,285 --> 00:28:01,036
You're sure they don't suspect you?

456
00:28:01,328 --> 00:28:02,454
Hundred percent.

457
00:28:02,580 --> 00:28:04,748
What are you so nervous
about, Vince?

458
00:28:05,875 --> 00:28:08,168
We never meant for you
to get released this early.

459
00:28:08,335 --> 00:28:10,254
And we never meant to kill that guard.

460
00:28:11,130 --> 00:28:13,674
We're improvising.
And I don't like that.

461
00:28:14,341 --> 00:28:15,968
It's all gonna work out.

462
00:28:17,386 --> 00:28:20,097
- You all set for tomorrow?
- We're good.

463
00:28:20,222 --> 00:28:23,100
Just bring the money down to the storage
basement, and I'll get it out of there.

464
00:28:23,726 --> 00:28:25,311
You're forgetting the last part.

465
00:28:31,025 --> 00:28:32,943
I don't wanna kill him.

466
00:28:34,028 --> 00:28:35,487
I know you don't.

467
00:28:37,406 --> 00:28:38,574
Put him on for me.

468
00:28:39,992 --> 00:28:41,368
I wanna say goodbye.

469
00:28:55,633 --> 00:28:57,051
Sloan. Please.

470
00:28:57,176 --> 00:28:58,928
For God's sake, you don't
have to do this.

471
00:28:59,053 --> 00:29:01,472
You could be a little more
convincing, Gary.

472
00:29:01,931 --> 00:29:06,602
- What did I ever do to you?
- You still don't understand, do you?

473
00:29:07,728 --> 00:29:10,230
"But that's always been
your problem, Gary."

474
00:29:10,731 --> 00:29:13,525
You wasted ten years of my life.

475
00:29:13,859 --> 00:29:17,905
You dragged me down with you.
Never again.

476
00:29:18,572 --> 00:29:20,908
- Sloan, please.
- Goodbye, Gary.

477
00:29:21,575 --> 00:29:23,035
Sloan, wait.

478
00:29:33,694 --> 00:29:34,778
It's a very sensitive mic.

479
00:29:34,903 --> 00:29:36,238
We'll be able to communicate
the whole time.

480
00:29:36,405 --> 00:29:37,823
You'll hear us, we'll hear you.

481
00:29:42,369 --> 00:29:43,871
Test, one-two.

482
00:29:44,079 --> 00:29:46,498
- Is that coming through?
- Yes. Yes.

483
00:29:48,876 --> 00:29:51,044
And we'll be nearby, in case anything
goes wrong.

484
00:29:51,712 --> 00:29:53,881
We won't be seen.
It'll just be our team, okay?

485
00:30:21,742 --> 00:30:24,953
- How are you doing, Sloan?
- Hanging in.

486
00:30:27,372 --> 00:30:28,916
We've got ten minutes till the pickup.

487
00:30:29,082 --> 00:30:30,125
Hang in there.

488
00:30:31,710 --> 00:30:33,003
Boss, what's happening?

489
00:30:34,296 --> 00:30:37,132
We're just sitting tight.
Nothing's going on.

490
00:30:38,759 --> 00:30:39,801
"Wait a minute."

491
00:30:40,302 --> 00:30:42,930
"I see somebody who fits
a description of the kidnapper."

492
00:30:45,474 --> 00:30:49,144
"It may be early, but I'm gonna get
a closer look, see if it's him."

493
00:30:51,021 --> 00:30:53,023
"It's definitely the kidnapper."

494
00:30:53,607 --> 00:30:55,984
- "I'm going in."
- Okay, I'm coming.

495
00:31:01,823 --> 00:31:02,866
"I'm on my way."

496
00:31:06,954 --> 00:31:09,748
- You can't arrest him.
- We can't risk him getting away.

497
00:31:10,123 --> 00:31:12,542
- What about Gary?
- We'll do everything we can, but...

498
00:31:12,668 --> 00:31:13,710
"He spotted me."

499
00:31:13,835 --> 00:31:15,587
- "Shots fired."
- "I'm almost there."

500
00:31:16,463 --> 00:31:17,547
"I've been hit."

501
00:31:17,673 --> 00:31:20,092
- Stay here.
- "I've been shot."

502
00:31:25,055 --> 00:31:27,766
Move in! I need... I need rescue. Please!

503
00:31:28,517 --> 00:31:29,851
- Okay, just bring it down...
- Hurry!

504
00:31:29,977 --> 00:31:31,103
Rigsby, car.

505
00:31:31,603 --> 00:31:33,689
It was a little over the top, okay?

506
00:31:37,150 --> 00:31:38,193
He's trying to get away!

507
00:31:38,318 --> 00:31:39,361
And cue gunshots.

508
00:31:42,072 --> 00:31:43,198
Returning fire.

509
00:31:45,367 --> 00:31:47,869
- And he's hit.
- "The kidnapper's down."

510
00:31:48,078 --> 00:31:49,413
"He's still alive."

511
00:31:49,621 --> 00:31:50,664
"We got him."

512
00:31:57,963 --> 00:31:59,256
That's good.

513
00:31:59,381 --> 00:32:01,425
You don't criticize his performance?
Just mine?

514
00:32:02,050 --> 00:32:03,885
He was good. You?

515
00:32:05,804 --> 00:32:08,390
I've got her. She's on the exterior.

516
00:32:09,641 --> 00:32:10,851
She's on the move.

517
00:32:12,269 --> 00:32:13,895
Heading toward the west entrance.

518
00:32:19,568 --> 00:32:21,069
Going down the escalators.

519
00:32:26,241 --> 00:32:28,994
She just went into the back corridor. B-7.

520
00:32:41,339 --> 00:32:42,382
Damn it.

521
00:32:43,133 --> 00:32:45,844
She just went into a dead zone.
She knew exactly where to go.

522
00:32:45,969 --> 00:32:47,512
South end of the mall. Move in now.

523
00:32:47,846 --> 00:32:49,097
Got it. Move.

524
00:33:11,620 --> 00:33:13,955
The kidnapper must've planted
her change of clothes here.

525
00:33:14,539 --> 00:33:17,417
She had an escape plan the whole time.
She knew things might go bad.

526
00:33:21,671 --> 00:33:23,298
There's only one number on the phone.

527
00:33:24,341 --> 00:33:25,884
Must be Sloan's accomplice.

528
00:33:27,302 --> 00:33:29,387
If we can trace his phone's
location, we can find him.

529
00:33:29,763 --> 00:33:30,806
Do it.

530
00:33:33,892 --> 00:33:35,811
Van Pelt. Trace this number for me.

531
00:33:40,398 --> 00:33:41,441
I got it.

532
00:33:41,566 --> 00:33:44,194
The kidnapper's still in the mall.
I t looks like he's in the storage basement.

533
00:33:50,992 --> 00:33:53,161
Freeze. Freeze!
Don't move! Don't move!

534
00:33:53,286 --> 00:33:54,746
Down on the ground now. Get down!

535
00:33:57,624 --> 00:33:58,792
Hands behind your back.

536
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:03,505
All right, stand up.

537
00:34:06,466 --> 00:34:07,759
Tell me where Gary is.

538
00:34:07,884 --> 00:34:08,927
Screw you.

539
00:34:10,345 --> 00:34:11,888
We know Sloan's behind this.

540
00:34:13,014 --> 00:34:14,432
You were just her puppet.

541
00:34:15,433 --> 00:34:17,644
Now, we may be able to go a little
easier on you

542
00:34:18,186 --> 00:34:19,896
but not unless you help us right now.

543
00:34:21,273 --> 00:34:22,315
It's over.

544
00:34:23,108 --> 00:34:24,276
Don't be stupid.

545
00:34:29,906 --> 00:34:33,201
He's in a warehouse.
Nine North Citrus Avenue.

546
00:35:02,262 --> 00:35:03,389
Don't move.

547
00:35:03,555 --> 00:35:04,598
Let me see your hands.

548
00:35:08,060 --> 00:35:09,228
Hands behind your back.

549
00:35:17,486 --> 00:35:18,695
How did you...

550
00:35:23,117 --> 00:35:24,368
Get her out of here.

551
00:35:34,253 --> 00:35:35,295
Gary!

552
00:35:38,757 --> 00:35:40,759
Oh, my God. I can't believe it.

553
00:35:41,677 --> 00:35:43,053
Thank you so much.

554
00:35:43,345 --> 00:35:45,264
- You all right?
- Yeah. No, I'm okay.

555
00:35:45,389 --> 00:35:46,515
It's so good to see you.

556
00:35:47,057 --> 00:35:49,017
- So we got Sloan.
- Mm.

557
00:35:49,143 --> 00:35:50,936
How did we know she was one
of the kidnappers?

558
00:35:51,478 --> 00:35:54,106
When we were negotiating
Vince had to hang up

559
00:35:54,231 --> 00:35:56,775
and talk to somebody before
making a counter-offer.

560
00:35:56,900 --> 00:35:58,694
We figured that person
was the mastermind

561
00:35:58,819 --> 00:36:00,487
and somebody who knew
the Goodwins well.

562
00:36:00,612 --> 00:36:03,365
So Jane asked Vince to release
a hostage.

563
00:36:03,490 --> 00:36:06,034
Whoever he released had to have
been his collaborator.

564
00:36:06,869 --> 00:36:10,289
- Amazing. Where is Jane?
- On a personal errand.

565
00:36:10,414 --> 00:36:13,000
Shoot. A few reporters
wanted to interview him.

566
00:36:13,167 --> 00:36:14,835
This is turning into a pretty big story.

567
00:36:15,544 --> 00:36:16,628
I could do it.

568
00:36:17,796 --> 00:36:19,923
Yeah, that's okay. I got it.

569
00:36:32,478 --> 00:36:33,729
Welcome home.

570
00:36:34,104 --> 00:36:35,689
What the hell are you doing here?

571
00:36:35,814 --> 00:36:37,983
Sorry, I... I didn't mean to alarm you.

572
00:36:39,067 --> 00:36:40,527
Get out of my house.

573
00:36:40,694 --> 00:36:42,613
I will in a moment.
But first we need to talk.

574
00:36:42,779 --> 00:36:46,617
- It's... It's important.
- I've got nothing to say to you.

575
00:36:48,619 --> 00:36:50,454
Then have a drink and listen.

576
00:37:03,634 --> 00:37:04,676
Please.

577
00:37:11,517 --> 00:37:12,893
I think you're in trouble, Walter.

578
00:37:14,394 --> 00:37:15,479
Wrong.

579
00:37:16,021 --> 00:37:17,481
I'm here to help you.

580
00:37:17,898 --> 00:37:19,942
Help me?
You don't even know me.

581
00:37:20,692 --> 00:37:24,029
I know that you still love your wife
even though she broke your heart.

582
00:37:24,905 --> 00:37:27,032
I know that you're very lonely.

583
00:37:28,909 --> 00:37:32,913
I know you're tormented by sexual desires
that make you feel ashamed of.

584
00:37:34,790 --> 00:37:36,291
I know you like scotch.

585
00:37:39,586 --> 00:37:40,837
Get out.

586
00:37:41,088 --> 00:37:44,967
I'm telling you this so that you know
that it's pointless lying to me.

587
00:37:45,467 --> 00:37:49,263
The FBI made you move Lorelei because
they had leverage over you, right?

588
00:37:49,555 --> 00:37:51,181
I said get out.

589
00:37:51,348 --> 00:37:55,143
They had leverage over you
because of a crime you committed.

590
00:37:55,978 --> 00:37:57,145
No.

591
00:37:57,854 --> 00:37:59,898
That's as good as a yes, Walter.

592
00:38:02,067 --> 00:38:04,027
You raped a woman, didn't you?

593
00:38:05,237 --> 00:38:06,488
No.

594
00:38:06,655 --> 00:38:08,031
An inmate.

595
00:38:08,490 --> 00:38:11,702
The FBI took that information
and they blackmailed you.

596
00:38:11,827 --> 00:38:14,246
And made you take
Lorelei on a mystery tour.

597
00:38:14,955 --> 00:38:16,540
I don't know what
you're talking about.

598
00:38:17,165 --> 00:38:20,210
You say that, but what you're thinking is
"How does he know this?"

599
00:38:21,003 --> 00:38:23,005
"How can he read my mind."

600
00:38:27,050 --> 00:38:30,679
And no, hitting me won't do you any good.

601
00:38:34,224 --> 00:38:35,809
You don't understand.

602
00:38:40,355 --> 00:38:43,775
I... I couldn't help myself.

603
00:38:47,821 --> 00:38:49,364
I'm so sorry.

604
00:38:51,158 --> 00:38:52,909
We all have our weaknesses, Walter.

605
00:38:56,038 --> 00:38:57,831
Who contacted you?

606
00:39:00,792 --> 00:39:02,502
A man called me on the phone.

607
00:39:05,005 --> 00:39:06,214
I never saw him.

608
00:39:06,757 --> 00:39:07,799
Name?

609
00:39:09,259 --> 00:39:10,510
Nemo.

610
00:39:11,678 --> 00:39:14,765
Said his name was FBI Agent Nemo.

611
00:39:14,890 --> 00:39:16,099
Oh, that's cute.

612
00:39:17,726 --> 00:39:19,686
Latin for nobody.

613
00:39:20,937 --> 00:39:22,439
Where did you take Lorelei?

614
00:39:22,606 --> 00:39:26,109
I promise, I'll never touch
another inmate. Never, I swear.

615
00:39:26,276 --> 00:39:29,196
I believe you, Walter.
Where did you take Lorelei?

616
00:39:30,489 --> 00:39:32,157
Look at me, Walter.

617
00:39:33,492 --> 00:39:35,243
You have a chance to make this right.

618
00:39:38,330 --> 00:39:40,248
Where did you take Lorelei?

619
00:39:46,546 --> 00:39:49,257
Okay. I'll tell you.

620
00:40:01,812 --> 00:40:03,313
He's all yours.
